Transportation Division of Transit & Rail and the
Federal Railroad Administration is nearing the end of
the of the Interregional Connectivity Study (ICS),
pictured at right, which examines:

High speed technologies: This study is
examining multiple types of high speed
technologies currently used in the U.S.,
Europe, and Asia.

Alignments (paths the high speed rail could
potentially follow): A variety of alignments
will be studied for each section of the study
area, and will consider impacts, design
feasibility, public input, benefits, and
technology. The use of current railroad
alignments may constrain the speed and type
of technology used.
